WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:05.740
The mind-blowing second season of The Umbrella
Academy is loaded with hidden details, comic

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.470
book easter eggs, and a trail of clues predicting
the big cliffhanger ending.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:13.709
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing everything you missed

00:00:13.709 --> 00:00:15.440
in The Umbrella Academy Season 2.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.849
Just before we begin, I want to thank the
sponsor of this video, Squarespace.

00:00:18.849 --> 00:00:22.070
More on why they're a great place to build
a website at the end.

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:25.279
Spoilers ahead so take care if you're not
caught up.

00:00:25.279 --> 00:00:29.750
One of the many great things about Season
2 was seeing Pogo again, this time as a baby,

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.529
and discovering that he was once a budding
astronaut.

00:00:32.529 --> 00:00:36.969
And there was a little easter egg to the chimpanzee's
time in space in the scene where Five tries

00:00:36.969 --> 00:00:39.290
to buy some candy from a vending machine.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:42.469
To the left of the candy that Five wants is
another chocolate bar called Pogo Gogos, with

00:00:42.469 --> 00:00:47.690
the slogan "Take flight with Pogo Gogos",
suggesting perhaps that after going into space

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:52.540
the astrochimp became something of a celebrity,
at least enough to get a chocolate bar name

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:53.540
after him.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:57.780
And take an even closer look at the candy
bar because there's a secret sparrow symbol

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:01.640
hidden inside one of the letters,
a sneaky easter egg to the rival team that

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:06.640
the Umbrella gang discover has taken their
place at the academy when they return to 2019.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:10.682
In fact, this secret sparrow is just one of
many clues planted throughout Season 2 that

00:01:10.682 --> 00:01:13.110
hint to the new Sparrow Academy.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:16.920
In the third episode, there's a sparrow on
the bath towel at the hotel where the Handler

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:20.290
is staying,
and when Lila is thinking about what to eat,

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:22.640
you can spot a little sparrow on the hotel
menu.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:27.509
Also a flock of birds, possibly sparrows,
form the Umbrella symbol for the opening titles

00:01:27.509 --> 00:01:28.509
of that episode.

00:01:28.509 --> 00:01:32.770
In addition to that, there's a sparrow on
a calendar at Allison and Ray's house.

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:36.369
And there are a couple of sparrow-like birds
in a picture frame on the wall of the meeting

00:01:36.369 --> 00:01:39.939
room where Five goes to kill the Commission's
board of directors.

00:01:39.939 --> 00:01:45.329
You can also see a sparrow symbol on the blackboard
inside Reginald Hargreeves' secret room.

00:01:45.329 --> 00:01:49.311
And when Old Man Five opens his briefcase
just before the Kennedy assassination, you

00:01:49.311 --> 00:01:54.200
can see a sparrow emblem on a paper just above
Vanya's book from Season 1.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:59.020
And then there's a small sparrow on the Kill
Order that the Handler issued for Lila's parents.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:04.149
In the finale, you can also spot the new Sparrow
Academy coat of arms on Ben's jacket and also

00:02:04.149 --> 00:02:06.150
on the wall behind Hargreeves.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:10.230
Some other interesting connections that certain
characters may have with the Sparrow Academy

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:14.160
are the Handler who wears a bath towel on
her head with a little bird on top,

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:19.070
and Sissy's son Harlan often plays with a
toy bird throughout Season 2 which we also

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:21.380
see him levitating in the finale.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:25.090
This is just a theory, but could Harlan grow
up to become the father of one of the Sparrow

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:26.320
Academy team?

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.300
And is the Handler or the Commission involved
at all in the formation of the Sparrows?

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.080
Given the sheer number of sparrow clues throughout
Season 2,

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:37.520
it's almost as if the creation of the Sparrow
Academy was inevitable the moment the Umbrella

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:41.200
Academy jumped back in time to the 60s and
began changing the timeline.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:46.301
In Season 2, Luther struggles with his situation
especially after he falls out with Jack Ruby

00:02:46.301 --> 00:02:49.780
and discovers that his crush Allison is happily
married with another man.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:53.470
So, he resorts to comfort eating as a way
of dealing with his unhappiness.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:57.400
The scenes of Luther cooking an enormous mound
of eggs or munching his way through plates

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:00.390
of BBQ
are a hat tip to the second volume of the

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:04.520
comic books in which Luther falls into a depression
and ends up becoming morbidly obese.

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:09.020
Tom Hopper, who plays Luther, told Nerdist
that the TV series decided against using a

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:13.310
"full-on fat suit" for his character as Marvel
did that recently in Avengers: Endgame with

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:14.310
Thor.

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:18.020
When Luther heads out for a run, the show
tips its hat to the training scenes in the

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:21.840
Rocky movies where Sylvester Stallone runs
through the streets in a grey tracksuit and

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.660
kids run along with him.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:28.200
Luther's running scene ends rather less victoriously
than Rocky's though as he trips and ends up

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:32.200
face-down on the ground after he mistakenly
thinks he's seen Allison.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:36.640
The Umbrella Academy's powers really level
up in Season 2 with Klaus mastering how to

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.780
manifest spirits in the real world.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:44.031
However, comic book Klaus also has the power
of levitation and Season 2 makes a funny reference

00:03:44.031 --> 00:03:48.280
to this when we see him floating miraculously
in mid-air in front of his cult,

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:52.870
the joke, of course, being that he's actually
being lifted up by the invisible Ben.

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:58.080
We get an awesome Five vs Five fight scene
in episode nine when schoolboy Five and Old

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:02.800
Man Five are gripped by a homicidal urge to
kill each other due to the effects of Paradox

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:03.800
Psychosis.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:08.260
The pair try to outmanoeuvre each other using
spatial jumps in a very cool scene appropriately

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:10.700
set to the tune of Dancing With Myself.

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:14.680
The scene is a nod to Avengers: Endgame where
Captain America travelled back in time and

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:16.850
ended up fighting with his past self.

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:20.840
And there's another homage to Captain America
when, during the fight, schoolboy Five drops

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:23.860
Steve Roger's iconic line:
"I can do this all day."

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:24.860
"I can do this all day."

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:25.860
"Yeah, I know.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:26.860
I know."

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:31.810
And, of course, both scenes are a wink to
fans of the 1960s animated Spider-Man cartoon

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:34.910
where the real Spidey faces off with a Spider-Man
imposter,

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:39.730
a moment that became a hugely popular meme
and was recently given a fresh twist in Spider-Man

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:41.410
into the Spider-Verse.

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:45.680
In Season 2, Diego's hero complex really takes
over as he becomes obsessed with trying to

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:46.960
save President Kennedy.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:51.130
But there was a little detail in the season's
opening scene you might have missed that sets

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:53.210
Diego apart from his siblings.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:57.380
Whereas everyone else crashed to the ground
when they dropped out of the sky in the 60s,

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:01.710
Diego instead managed a stylish superhero
landing, very much in character with his hero

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:02.710
complex.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:03.710
"Superhero landing!

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:05.350
You know, that's really hard on your knees."

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:10.340
The Handler made a surprise return in Season
2 proving herself an outrageously ruthless

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:11.340
villain.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:15.510
And one of the biggest WTF moments came when
she decided to end A.J.'s attempts to interfere

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:20.070
with her plans once and for all, by grabbing
the goldfish and swallowing him whole.

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:23.960
This is actually a shout-out to the comics
where Five took his revenge on the goldfish

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:26.820
head of the Commission, Carmichael, by eating
him alive.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:31.170
However, in a brief flashback scene where
the Handler stamps the kill order for Lila's

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:36.710
parents, if you look very closely, just above
the stamp you can see A.J.'s full name: Atlas

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:38.770
Jericho Carmichael.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:42.520
Also on the desk next to the kill order, you
can just make out the corner of a receipt

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:44.120
from Griddy's Doughnuts.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:48.370
Griddy's is the donut shop from the first
season where Hazel met and fell in love with

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:49.370
Agnes.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:54.270
In Season 2, human Grace discovers a hidden
room filled with Reginald Hargreeves' research.

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:58.080
And on the blackboard are plans for something
called "The Televator", which is described

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:00.380
as "the next great mode of transportation".

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:04.760
In the comics, the Televator is a machine
invented by Hargreeves and Klaus has one built

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:08.240
to transport him, Luther and Pogo from Vietnam
to Dallas.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:12.330
The Televator easter egg in the TV show might
be a hint that we'll see this device in a

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:16.960
future season, especially given it also made
an appearance on a comic-book cover in Season

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:17.960
1.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:22.170
And there's an easter egg to another Hargreeves
invention from the comics, this time the breakfast

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:26.640
cereal Clever Crisp, which appears on the
kitchen table in Elliot's home.

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:30.570
Another comic book easter egg crops up when
Five complains that his siblings failed to

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:34.890
show up for their time jump back to 2019:
"All we had to do was be here.

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:37.070
Didn't have to fight a giant sea monster,
no."

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:40.740
This is a nod to the comic book short story
"But the Past Ain't Through With You" where

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:44.540
the Umbrella Academy were delayed on a mission
after having to battle a sea serpent in the

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:45.550
Pacific Ocean.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:51.690
Just before the Umbrella gang return from
1963 to 2019, we see a brief scene of Jack

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:54.020
Ruby watching a news report about the Kennedy
assassination.

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:59.190
Then there's a very quick shot of him grabbing
a gun, a subtle reference to how in real life

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:03.510
Ruby fatally shot Lee Harvey Oswald while
he was in Dallas police custody.

00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:07.860
Oswald was the primary suspect in the Kennedy
murder investigation at the time, and Ruby

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:11.920
claimed he shot him spontaneously and that
he was upset over Kennedy's death.

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:16.681
There are many conspiracy theories surrounding
the JFK assassination and the Umbrella Academy

00:07:16.681 --> 00:07:20.940
show mines a number of those to set up various
subplots in Season 2.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:25.750
For example, the Umbrella Man, who the team
mistakenly believe is their father is a real-life

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:29.419
person who was standing near Kennedy's motorcade
when the president was shot.

00:07:29.419 --> 00:07:33.130
Because the real-life Umbrella Man was wearing
a large raincoat and carrying an umbrella

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:37.060
on a warm, sunny day in Dallas,
some believe he was there to act as a signal

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:41.540
for the assassination to go ahead, something
that was also referenced in The Umbrella Academy.

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:43.540
"..he's the signalman for the whole goddamn
thing."

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:47.730
The theory was called into question when Louie
Steven Witt came forward to state that he

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:51.230
was the Umbrella Man on the day
and that he was carrying the umbrella to protest

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:56.020
the Kennedy family's appeasement policy towards
Nazi Germany in the 30s.

00:07:56.020 --> 00:08:01.000
In the show, the shadowy Majestic 12 organisation
turns out to be behind JFK's murder.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:06.070
In real-life, the Majestic 12 are a purported
secret organisation whose existence is popular

00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:10.340
among UFO conspiracy theorists,
although the FBI and others say the existence

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.380
of the secret society is a hoax.

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:16.290
Among the alleged real-life members of the
group is Roscoe H. Hillenkoetter who was the

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:17.290
first director of the CIA.

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:20.960
He's referenced in the show on an invitation
card to the gala at the Mexican Consulate,

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:24.320
which is where we see the Majestic 12 meet
for the first time.

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:28.510
The TV show plays up the nefarious nature
of the Majestic 12 and how they seem to be

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:30.480
secretly influencing events.

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:34.190
The sunglasses man often pops up in the background
of various scenes.

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:38.120
For example, he seems to be on friendly terms
with Jack Ruby when we see the club owner

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:41.570
briefly talking to him in the first episode
"You OK here?"

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:45.980
Could this be the show suggesting a connection
between the Majestic 12 and Jack Ruby's subsequent

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:47.460
murder of Lee Harvey Oswald?

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:51.850
And the same sunglasses man is watching on
during Pogo's astronaut training.

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:56.170
He's a bit of an enigma and the way he seems
to be constantly smoking reminds me of The

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:58.410
Smoking Man from The X-Files.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:03.490
And the X-Files gets its own shout-out when
conspiracy theorist Elliott first meets Five

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:08.529
and asks if UFOs and crop circles are real,
and Five replies using the famous tagline

00:09:08.529 --> 00:09:12.150
from the sci-fi TV series:
"Well, the truth is out there."

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:16.250
And given Elliott's interest in spaceships
and aliens, I can't help but wonder if his

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:18.630
character was named after the little boy,
Elliot,

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:21.960
who befriended an extra-terrestrial in E.T.

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:26.130
Even before it's revealed that Reginald Hargreeves
is an alien in season 2's penultimate episode,

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:28.510
there are little hints at his true form.

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:33.870
For example, Diego warns Grace about Hargreeves
"and his nasty squad of lizard people".

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:38.480
And costume designer Christopher Hargadon
told Nerdist that he specifically gave Hargreeves

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:41.010
"lizard shoes"
and more vibrant clothes than his colleagues

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:44.610
as he wanted to indicate that there was "something
strange about the guy".

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:48.370
And the face mask that Hargreeves removes
from his head is also a reference to the same

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:51.680
mask that reveals his alien origins in the
comics.

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:55.640
The season finale reveals the apparent end
of the Umbrella Academy and their replacement

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:56.930
with the Sparrow Academy.

00:09:56.930 --> 00:10:01.580
And the episode's title "The End of Something"
is a clever call-back to the first season

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:05.390
when the Handler cryptically explained to
Five that the apocalypse wasn't the end of

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:06.430
everything but..

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:08.690
"Just the end of... something."

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:13.610
Now, you doubtless noticed the Handler's outfits
getting more and more flamboyant as the season

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:16.060
progressed and her power grew within the Commission.

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:19.370
But there were some more subtle details that
also mirrored her rise to power.

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:24.820
For example, in the third episode you can
spot a small red spider brooch on her handbag.

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:29.390
By the ninth episode there's a bigger spider
brooch and it's migrated onto her outfit and

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:32.200
by the finale it's climbed all the way up
to her hat

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:36.830
The spiders seem to reflect the ever-growing
web that the Handler spins in Season 2 as

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:38.770
her status rises.

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:42.770
And the red sequined shoes that the camera
focusses on when the Handler arrives during

00:10:42.770 --> 00:10:46.520
the murder of Lila's parents
are a possible allusion to the Ruby Slippers

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:50.760
from the Wizard of Oz which originally belonged
to the Wicked Witch of the East.

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:54.550
The song "Bibbidi-Bobbidi-Boo" which plays
when the Handler returns to the Commission

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:57.510
is a subtle reference to Cinderella's Fairy
Godmother,

00:10:57.510 --> 00:11:02.340
the twist here being that for Lila the Handler
ends up being a wicked mother to her who deliberately

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:04.600
orchestrated the murder of her parents.

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:09.490
Lila's ability to copy or mirror the Umbrella
crew's powers is a pretty awesome reveal in

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:14.290
the final episode, and when Fives asks her
how she can do it, she simply replies

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:18.290
"Anything you can do, I can do better"
Which is a little reference to the duet of

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:22.120
the same name from the musical Annie Get Your
Gun where the two singers compete to outdo

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:23.850
each other performing the same tasks.

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:28.649
There's a neat bit of foreshadowing of Harlan's
arc when in the opening episode Vanya tells

00:11:28.649 --> 00:11:32.270
Sissy that she and Harlan have been reading
James and the Giant Peach.

00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:36.370
In the popular novel by Roald Dahl, a young
boy ends up going on a fantastical adventure

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:41.510
with seven magical bugs, a possible parallel
to Harlan and the seven members of the Umbrella

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:42.510
Academy.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:44.380
"I know you don't get it, but that is an excellent
reference."

00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:48.500
And after Harlan becomes connected to Vanya
through the powers that she transfers to him,

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:52.000
he seems to have some foresight or ability
to sense the future.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:55.940
In the eighth episode, you can see Harlan
drawing a picture of somebody flying above

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:59.420
the farmhouse and barn,
a foreshadowing of how Vanya will later float

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:03.360
out of the barn to attack the Handler's army
of Commission agents in the finale.

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:07.950
There've been plenty of comparisons between
The Umbrella Academy and other popular superhero

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:12.630
teams such as the X-Men and Doom Patrol,
with Vanya's powerful abilities that sometimes

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:17.410
threaten to rage out of control often reminding
people of Jean Grey and Dark Phoenix.

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:21.830
And it feels like there's a Jean Grey-esque
moment in Season 2 when Vanya levitates the

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:24.520
water out of the lake where Harlan drowns.

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:29.550
Ellen Page who plays Vanya joined the X-Men
movies as Kitty Pryde in X-Men The Last Stand,

00:12:29.550 --> 00:12:33.900
and in that film when the Phoenix force rages
out of control in Jean Grey, she levitates

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:36.760
a wall of water around Alcatraz.

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:41.140
And suitably for a time-travel apocalypse
story, The Umbrella Academy also squeezes

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:46.210
in a reference to the Terminator movies when
Hazel shows up in the midst of the 1963 doomsday

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:48.870
and tells Five:
"If you wanna live, come with me."

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:52.980
I just love the incredible attention to detail
in the series and all the creative easter

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:54.520
eggs added for the fans.

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:58.420
And if you feel inspired by the show's inventiveness,
give an outlet to your own imagination on

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:04.000
Squarespace, a fantastic platform that you
can easily use to build your own online presence.

